scope: |
  specs/ssc3-jit.md §10.1 asks whoever gets a quiet machine to re-run J1b, J1c and J1d. J1d was
  re-run (4584fe61d), J1b came back a WIN and overturned the board (7fe1b7525). This slice takes
  the remaining two, and it starts with J2 rather than J1c on purpose: J2's lane is LIVE behind
  `ssc3 exec --closures`, so it is one binary and no port, while J1c's executor lane was reverted
  out of a file that has since gained 373 lines. J2's verdict is also the least trustworthy in the
  ladder -- it was taken at host load 69-96, the loudest run in the whole history.
next: record the J2 quiet re-measurement, then state the J1c position with its port cost
